# QGroundControl Multi-Vehicle Management System

## Vehicle Management Architecture

### Vehicle Discovery Pattern
```cpp
// In MissionService::generateWaypointsFromPosition()
MultiVehicleManager* multiVehicleManager = MultiVehicleManager::instance();
QmlObjectListModel* vehiclesModel = multiVehicleManager->vehicles();

QList<Vehicle*> nonId1Vehicles;
for (int i = 0; i < vehiclesModel->count(); i++) {
    Vehicle* vehicle = qobject_cast<Vehicle*>(vehiclesModel->get(i));
    if (vehicle && vehicle->id() != 1) {
        nonId1Vehicles.append(vehicle);
    }
}
```

### Vehicle Filtering Logic
- **Vehicle ID 1**: Reserved for special observation mission
- **Other Vehicles**: Used for waypoint distribution
- **Validation**: Check for valid vehicle objects before processing

## Mission Assignment Patterns

### Altitude Separation Strategy
```cpp
// Set different altitude for each drone to avoid collisions
int vehicleAltitude = altitude + (i * 10); // 10m altitude difference per drone

// Check vehicle's maximum altitude parameter
double maxAltitude = 50.0; // Conservative default
if (vehicle->parameterManager()->parameterExists(-1, "MPC_ALT_MAX")) {
    Fact* maxAltFact = vehicle->parameterManager()->getParameter(-1, "MPC_ALT_MAX");
    double paramMaxAltitude = maxAltFact->rawValue().toDouble();
    if (paramMaxAltitude > 0) {
        maxAltitude = paramMaxAltitude * 0.8; // Use 80% for safety margin
    }
}
```

### Mission Type Assignment
- **Vehicle ID 1**: Observation/Loiter mission
- **Vehicle ID 2+**: Waypoint missions with distributed waypoints
- **Altitude Separation**: 10m between each vehicle level

## Vehicle State Management

### Active Vehicle Handling
```cpp
// Get active vehicle for reference
Vehicle* activeVehicle = multiVehicleManager->activeVehicle();
if (!activeVehicle) {
    emit missionGenerationCompleted(false, "No active vehicle");
    return;
}

// Use active vehicle's position as reference
QGeoCoordinate vehiclePosition = activeVehicle->coordinate();
```

### Vehicle Validation Patterns
```cpp
// Validate vehicle before operations
if (!vehicle) {
    qDebug() << "WARNING - Invalid vehicle at index" << i;
    continue;
}

if (!vehicle->coordinate().isValid()) {
    qCWarning(MissionServiceLog) << "Vehicle" << vehicle->id() << "has invalid coordinates";
    continue;
}
```

## Mission Upload Patterns

### Per-Vehicle Mission Creation
```cpp
// Create mission for each vehicle
for (int i = 0; i < nonId1Vehicles.size() && i < distributedWaypoints.size(); i++) {
    Vehicle* vehicle = nonId1Vehicles[i];
    QList<QGeoCoordinate> vehicleWaypoints = distributedWaypoints[i];
    
    // Create mission items
    createTakeoffItem(vehicle, vehiclePosition, vehicleAltitude);
    createWaypointItems(vehicle, vehicleWaypoints, vehicleAltitude);
    createLandItem(vehicle, vehiclePosition, vehicleAltitude);
}
```

### Mission Item Creation
```cpp
// Takeoff item
void createTakeoffItem(Vehicle* vehicle, const QGeoCoordinate& position, int altitude) {
    MissionItem* takeoffItem = new MissionItem(vehicle->missionManager()->mission());
    takeoffItem->setCommand(MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF);
    takeoffItem->setCoordinate(position);
    takeoffItem->setParam7(altitude);
}

// Waypoint items
void createWaypointItems(Vehicle* vehicle, const QList<QGeoCoordinate>& waypoints, int altitude) {
    for (const QGeoCoordinate& waypoint : waypoints) {
        MissionItem* wpItem = new MissionItem(vehicle->missionManager()->mission());
        wpItem->setCommand(MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT);
        wpItem->setCoordinate(waypoint);
        wpItem->setParam7(altitude);
    }
}
```

## Special Mission Handling

### Vehicle ID 1 Observation Mission
```cpp
// Calculate safe observation position
QGeoCoordinate safePosition = m_ptahMissionGenerator->calculateSafeObservationPosition(
    missionCenter, waypoints, altitude + 20);

// Create observation mission
createTakeoffItem(vehicle1, vehicle1Position, altitude + 20);
createLoiterItem(vehicle1, safePosition, altitude + 20);
createLandItem(vehicle1, vehicle1Position, altitude + 20);
```

### Safe Position Calculation
```cpp
// In PtahMissionGenerator::calculateSafeObservationPosition()
QGeoCoordinate PtahMissionGenerator::calculateSafeObservationPosition(
    const QGeoCoordinate& missionCenter, 
    const QList<QGeoCoordinate>& waypoints, 
    int altitude)
{
    // Calculate mission area bounds
    double minLat = waypoints[0].latitude();
    double maxLat = waypoints[0].latitude();
    double minLng = waypoints[0].longitude();
    double maxLng = waypoints[0].longitude();
    
    for (const QGeoCoordinate& coord : waypoints) {
        minLat = qMin(minLat, coord.latitude());
        maxLat = qMax(maxLat, coord.latitude());
        minLng = qMin(minLng, coord.longitude());
        maxLng = qMax(maxLng, coord.longitude());
    }
    
    // Calculate safe distance and position
    double latSpan = maxLat - minLat;
    double lngSpan = maxLng - minLng;
    double safeDistance = qMax(latSpan, lngSpan) * 1.5; // 50% safety margin
    
    // Position observer outside mission area
    QGeoCoordinate safePosition = missionCenter;
    safePosition.setLatitude(missionCenter.latitude() - safeDistance);
    safePosition.setAltitude(altitude);
    
    return safePosition;
}
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### Vehicle Connection Validation
```cpp
// Check if vehicles are connected and ready
if (vehiclesModel->count() == 0) {
    emit missionGenerationCompleted(false, "No vehicles connected");
    return;
}

if (nonId1Vehicles.isEmpty()) {
    emit missionGenerationCompleted(false, "No NON ID 1 vehicles found");
    return;
}
```

### Mission Upload Error Handling
```cpp
// Handle mission upload failures
connect(vehicle->missionManager(), &MissionManager::newMissionItemsAvailable,
        this, [this, vehicle](bool success) {
    if (!success) {
        qCWarning(MissionServiceLog) << "Failed to upload mission to vehicle" << vehicle->id();
        emit missionUploadFailed(vehicle->id(), "Mission upload failed");
    } else {
        qCDebug(MissionServiceLog) << "Mission uploaded successfully to vehicle" << vehicle->id();
        emit missionUploadCompleted(vehicle->id());
    }
});
```

